# Headers for the app and its files, served as static assets (the Worker's own
# replies, under /api/, set theirs in code: lib/http.ts). Only what cannot break
# a feature: no other site may frame Jarvis to trick a click out of someone, no
# file is read as a type it is not, and no <base> or plugin can be slipped in.
# A script and connect policy would have to list every source the app reaches
# (OpenAI, Google, Spotify's images, a family's own MCP servers), so it has none.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
